    {
      "id": "claim_2bfaf4aaba694eb4af3be1ff8accdb30",
      "statement": "gdelt.py, triage.py, research.py, verify.py, and prices.py each define hardcoded, non-env-configurable constants that materially bound pipeline behavior: gdelt.py's UPDATES (24), TOP_STORIES (30) and MARKET_THEMES set which GKG rows and how many stories enter the pipeline; triage.py's KEEP (3) and RUBRIC define the top-N cut and severity wording with no minimum severity floor; research.py's MAX_SEARCHES (3), MEMORY_DAYS (7), the 1500-character excerpt truncation, and recursion_limit (20) bound search volume, recall window, visible article text, and per-story agent steps; verify.py's SURE/DOUBT/SECTOR_SURE thresholds (0.7/0.4/0.75) and SECTORS set gate claim retention/flagging and the fixed sector vocabulary; prices.py's SECTOR_ETFS maps each sector to its SPDR ETF ticker and must stay in sync with verify.py's SECTORS.",
      "evidence": [
