    {
      "id": "claim_c4233ef30412404287609c5d1f72346b",
      "statement": "The graph uses a linear node chain (gdelt -> triage -> research -> verify -> price -> output, with follow-ups entering directly at research) and main.py persists checkpoints and the findings store in the same SQLite file data/threads.db, so a required-variable failure partway through a run leaves earlier nodes' state already checkpointed and resumable via `uv run main.py --thread <id>` once the missing/invalid key is fixed.",
